WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.662
Testing helps us check whether code behaves the way we expect.

00:00:03.662 --> 00:00:09.297
In beginner Python, assert is a simple way to start testing.

00:00:09.297 --> 00:00:13.302
On this slide, we define a function called normalize_status.

00:00:13.302 --> 00:00:18.262
The function strips extra spaces and converts the text to lowercase.

00:00:18.262 --> 00:00:21.067
Then we write three assert statements.

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:24.617
Each assert statement checks one expected behavior.

00:00:24.617 --> 00:00:29.517
The first test checks that Complete with extra spaces becomes complete.

00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:32.727
The second checks that CANCELLED becomes cancelled.

00:00:32.727 --> 00:00:36.982
The third checks that pending with a leading space becomes pending.

00:00:36.982 --> 00:00:42.242
If all assertions are true, the program prints All checks passed.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:47.777
Try changing one expected value to something incorrect and run the cell again.

00:00:47.777 --> 00:00:50.747
Python should raise an AssertionError.

00:00:50.747 --> 00:00:56.320
That error is helpful because it tells us the behavior no longer matches our expectation.
